WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.710 --> 00:00:05.450
If you really want to hear about just the
worst of the worst of the left, you have to

00:00:05.450 --> 00:00:08.830
hear about what's happening over the last
72 hours.

00:00:08.830 --> 00:00:14.059
Now, last week, I got a phone call during
live calls on last Friday show from a viewer

00:00:14.059 --> 00:00:19.869
asking me, what do I think about the AOC versus
Jimmy Dorje debate?

00:00:19.869 --> 00:00:23.570
And when the caller asked me about it, I had
no idea what it was about.

00:00:23.570 --> 00:00:28.240
And the caller explained to me very, very
politely, the debate is that a YouTube named

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:36.000
Jimmy Dorje thinks that the squad should hold
their votes for Nancy Pelosi's speaker of

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:41.629
speakership hostage unless Nancy Pelosi is
willing to hold a vote in the House for Medicare

00:00:41.629 --> 00:00:42.629
for all.

00:00:42.629 --> 00:00:45.839
And when the caller brought it up, I hadn't
heard about it at the time.

00:00:45.839 --> 00:00:48.269
It started on Twitter the previous weekend.

00:00:48.269 --> 00:00:50.609
I don't watch the show that the caller mentioned.

00:00:50.609 --> 00:00:53.539
I wasn't on Twitter over the over that weekend,
so I had no idea.

00:00:53.539 --> 00:00:56.879
I have now learned about it thanks to the
caller.

00:00:56.879 --> 00:01:00.110
And the same thing continued to explode this
weekend.

00:01:00.110 --> 00:01:04.710
We're now even AOC apparently isn't progressive
enough.

00:01:04.710 --> 00:01:12.030
AOC is failing progressive purity tests because
she's unsure about the value of holding her

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:15.310
vote hostage for a Medicare for all vote in
the House.

00:01:15.310 --> 00:01:20.140
She's questioning whether that would really
do anything for people with acute needs right

00:01:20.140 --> 00:01:21.140
now.

00:01:21.140 --> 00:01:24.170
Now, the funny thing about all of this is
that there's a bunch of funny things and some

00:01:24.170 --> 00:01:26.520
sad things and so infuriating things.

00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:30.880
One of the funny things about this is that
for the last several years, when it comes

00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:38.080
to AOC, I've mostly been attacked for being
too critical of AOC and for not being deferential

00:01:38.080 --> 00:01:40.560
enough to any of these notions.

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:44.509
When I found that she lacked knowledge or
pragmatism in one place or another, I would

00:01:44.509 --> 00:01:46.700
mention that people would be furious with
me.

00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:52.570
Now, AOC is actually the one being pragmatic
and the so-called populist left has turned

00:01:52.570 --> 00:01:53.570
on her.

00:01:53.570 --> 00:01:59.900
And what's really bonkers is that the populist
left seems more angry with AOC than they are

00:01:59.900 --> 00:02:01.189
with Donald Trump.

00:02:01.189 --> 00:02:06.340
When Trump is going lunatic, authoritarian
and had an Oval Office meeting over the weekend

00:02:06.340 --> 00:02:10.610
about whether he should declare martial law
if he even could, whether he should seize

00:02:10.610 --> 00:02:15.160
voting machines by force because he lost an
election and he can't admit it.

00:02:15.160 --> 00:02:18.470
But the populist left on Twitter is focused
on AOK now.

00:02:18.470 --> 00:02:23.650
In fact, I actually said about seven to eight
months after AOK was sworn in.

00:02:23.650 --> 00:02:30.360
You know, guys, I have to tell you, I am pleased
that Aoki's political instincts are maturing.

00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:36.320
Since she's gotten into Congress, her political
instincts improved dramatically from the campaign

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:39.290
AOC to when she was actually in office.

00:02:39.290 --> 00:02:44.880
Her pragmatism and her understanding of how
politics works improved dramatically.

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:49.130
And now, if you said to me right now, what
is the most important thing to keep in mind

00:02:49.130 --> 00:02:50.590
about this issue?

00:02:50.590 --> 00:02:56.090
What is the most instructive, possible takeaway
about this spat that is taking place within

00:02:56.090 --> 00:02:58.250
the left, mostly on Twitter and Reddit?

00:02:58.250 --> 00:03:00.350
Well, there's actually a few takeaways.

00:03:00.350 --> 00:03:03.790
Number one, there is nothing wrong with.

00:03:03.790 --> 00:03:07.890
I want people to take out a notepad and make
a note of what I'm about to say and don't

00:03:07.890 --> 00:03:13.890
email me about it, OK, because I'm telling
you right now there's nothing wrong with people

00:03:13.890 --> 00:03:16.410
on the left criticizing others on the left.

00:03:16.410 --> 00:03:17.560
Nothing wrong with that.

00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:23.070
There's nothing wrong with progressives, primarily
centrist or corporate Democrats.

00:03:23.070 --> 00:03:24.070
That should be.

00:03:24.070 --> 00:03:25.070
That's great.

00:03:25.070 --> 00:03:26.070
That should be encouraged.

00:03:26.070 --> 00:03:27.070
OK, great.

00:03:27.070 --> 00:03:30.140
There's nothing wrong with any of those things
at a structural level.

00:03:30.140 --> 00:03:36.000
But the takeaways here are, number one, the
so-called populist left on Twitter.

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:44.630
And Reddit represents a small but very vocal
Internet enclave that does not connect to

00:03:44.630 --> 00:03:46.910
most of what's happening in the real world.

00:03:46.910 --> 00:03:48.660
Now, we learned this sadly.

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:52.290
It was a rude awakening during the Democratic
primary.

00:03:52.290 --> 00:03:54.740
How could Bernie possibly have lost?

00:03:54.740 --> 00:03:56.510
He had so much energy.

00:03:56.510 --> 00:03:58.400
He had the best streams.

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:00.190
He had the best rallies.

00:04:00.190 --> 00:04:04.200
If you spent time on Twitter and Reddit, it
looked like Bernie couldn't possibly have

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:06.050
lost that primary.

00:04:06.050 --> 00:04:11.000
But he lost the primary by millions of votes
because most of the electorate and the Democratic

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:15.320
Party voters are not in the Internet populist
left space.

00:04:15.320 --> 00:04:17.030
It's not a value judgment.

00:04:17.030 --> 00:04:19.030
It's an evaluation of fact.

00:04:19.030 --> 00:04:22.740
And if we don't get it, it'll continue to
go this way.

00:04:22.740 --> 00:04:24.169
And this is the exact same thing.

00:04:24.169 --> 00:04:28.880
If you're a factory worker, dad, who's trying
to figure out how to put food on your family's

00:04:28.880 --> 00:04:33.710
table for your two kids while continuing to
work during a pandemic, and your employer

00:04:33.710 --> 00:04:37.600
might have to lay off 10 percent of the workforce
due to the pandemic and you might be in that

00:04:37.600 --> 00:04:38.960
10 percent laid off.

00:04:38.960 --> 00:04:44.280
Do you need a list of the members of Congress
who support Medicare for all right now, particularly

00:04:44.280 --> 00:04:50.020
absent any actual credible way to get it passed
as we are about to get a new Congress seated?

00:04:50.020 --> 00:04:52.469
I'm not saying the dad doesn't care about
Medicare.

00:04:52.469 --> 00:04:53.590
Get Medicare for all.

00:04:53.590 --> 00:04:55.930
I'm not saying that dad wouldn't benefit from
Medicare.

00:04:55.930 --> 00:04:57.400
For all I'm saying.

00:04:57.400 --> 00:05:01.910
Does anyone outside of these online spaces
think that what is effectively a naughty and

00:05:01.910 --> 00:05:07.729
nice list in a Congress that has two weeks
left before some some leave and some new people

00:05:07.729 --> 00:05:11.409
get sworn in, that's what that dad cares about.

00:05:11.409 --> 00:05:17.889
Or imagine a business owner in Houston who
sells wedding dresses, OK, and has seen their

00:05:17.889 --> 00:05:21.120
business decimated due to this due to the
pandemic.

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:22.819
They're waiting on a second stimulus.

00:05:22.819 --> 00:05:26.099
They're wondering when will people go back
to weddings?

00:05:26.099 --> 00:05:30.910
That business owner is waiting on a vote on
Medicare for all, which there is not even

00:05:30.910 --> 00:05:35.870
support for in the Senate anyway, and which
Joe Biden didn't run on what just to have

00:05:35.870 --> 00:05:37.840
a list of people to primary.

00:05:37.840 --> 00:05:42.009
So the point isn't that there's no place for
such a vote or that it shouldn't be done.

00:05:42.009 --> 00:05:43.580
I'm fine with it.

00:05:43.580 --> 00:05:50.120
But attacking AOC now, because she's far more
realistic about how politics works than much

00:05:50.120 --> 00:05:54.351
of the populist left, when we're we're trying
to get a second stimulus, it looks like we're

00:05:54.351 --> 00:05:56.380
going to get a pathetic one.

00:05:56.380 --> 00:05:58.979
And we have so many other issues going on.

00:05:58.979 --> 00:06:03.569
And again, the president is talking about
martial law and seizing voting machines.

00:06:03.569 --> 00:06:06.779
The point is, AOC now is not left enough.

00:06:06.779 --> 00:06:09.180
She's not passed the progressive purity test.

00:06:09.180 --> 00:06:11.960
It's another example of the left eating itself.

00:06:11.960 --> 00:06:14.330
If these people are even on the left, I'm
not sure.

00:06:14.330 --> 00:06:17.139
And that's what's tricky about populist rhetoric.

00:06:17.139 --> 00:06:21.300
It sounds very similar on the left and right
until you get to the solutions.

00:06:21.300 --> 00:06:28.729
Some of the so-called populist left now attacking
AOC is praising Tulsi Gabbard, whose recent

00:06:28.729 --> 00:06:34.449
ideas on trans people and abortion don't look
like anything I recognize as being part of

00:06:34.449 --> 00:06:35.449
the left.

00:06:35.449 --> 00:06:39.610
So maybe the issue and I'm thinking out loud
here, maybe the issue is that some of these

00:06:39.610 --> 00:06:41.560
people aren't really leftists.

00:06:41.560 --> 00:06:45.520
They seem more into what Tucker Carlson is
proposing than what we see from AOC.

00:06:45.520 --> 00:06:49.560
Now, again, there are people who say, I'm
not really on the left.

00:06:49.560 --> 00:06:54.500
So starting to to say, well, this person is
not really what they claim to be.

00:06:54.500 --> 00:06:57.069
I get that it's fraught and that it's problematic.

00:06:57.069 --> 00:07:01.509
And my point, again, just to restate it, is
not that the left shouldn't criticize the

00:07:01.509 --> 00:07:06.099
left when the left fails to be left, as I've
done many times.

00:07:06.099 --> 00:07:12.479
But the real issue here is that it seems to
be a complete loss of the plot for lack of

00:07:12.479 --> 00:07:14.810
a better term.

00:07:14.810 --> 00:07:19.900
Trump considering martial law and people are
saying AOC being unwilling to do something

00:07:19.900 --> 00:07:23.759
that will make no political difference anyway
makes her enemy number one.

00:07:23.759 --> 00:07:24.889
This is how the left keeps losing.

00:07:24.889 --> 00:07:25.889
I want the left to win.

00:07:25.889 --> 00:07:29.319
I don't think this is the path to victory.

00:07:29.319 --> 00:07:30.319
Let me know what you think.

00:07:30.319 --> 00:07:31.570
I would love to hear from you.

